*Source-Available • Non-Commercial Community Use • Paid API (Free Tier) • Paid Closed-Source Self-Hosting Commercial License Available • Full-Source Self-Hosting Free (OCL or OSI-Approved OSS) • Privacy-by-Design Required*

---

> **Note on terminology.** OCL is a *source-available* license, **not** an OSI-approved open source license: it permits commercial self-hosting only on the paid closed-source path or the free full-source path (Section 2A(b)). When this document refers to the "free full-source path," it means releasing the ENTIRE stack under OCL **or** an OSI-approved open source license — not that OCL itself is OSI-approved open source.

> **Definition of "Oxiverse Software."** "Oxiverse Software" (or "the Software") means the Oxiverse codebase and **all Oxiverse services — current and future** — that Licensor releases under this License, including but not limited to RAVANA, IntentForge, and any successor or additional services. New Oxiverse services are automatically covered by OCL; no separate agreement is needed for each.

### 1. Grant of License

Subject to the terms of this License, Likhith Sai Seemala ("Licensor") grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to:

* (a) use, copy, modify, and run the Software;
* (b) create derivative works of the Software;
* (c) share the Software and derivative works, **for Non-Commercial Purposes only**.

Derivative works created under this License must also be distributed under OCL v1.x and may not be relicensed under more permissive terms.

**For the avoidance of doubt, this Section 1 distinguishes between two scenarios:**

* **(i) Core Modifications.** Modifying, forking, extending, or creating derivative works of the Software's source code (including its cognitive architecture, components, and any part of the codebase) constitutes a derivative work and must remain under OCL v1.x. Such modifications may not be relicensed, sublicensed, or distributed under different terms.

* **(ii) Service Consumption.** Independently developed applications, products, or services that merely consume, interact with, or depend on the Software through its hosted services, APIs, or platform interfaces—without copying, modifying, or incorporating the Software's source code—are **not** considered derivative works of the Software, and are **not** subject to OCL's licensing restrictions. You may license, distribute, and monetize your independent product under **any terms you choose**—including a proprietary or closed-source license, an OSI-approved open source license (e.g., MIT, Apache 2.0, GPL), or OCL v1.x. No Commercial License from Licensor is required (see Section 2A(a)).

