### 2. Non-Commercial Use Definition

**"Non-Commercial Purpose"** means use that is:

* Personal, non-monetized experimentation
* Educational or academic instruction
* Academic or non-profit research
* Internal evaluation within a non-revenue-generating organization
* Open research or community learning projects

**Non-Commercial Purpose expressly excludes:**

* Selling, licensing, or monetizing the Software or derivatives
* Offering the Software as a hosted service (SaaS, API-as-a-Service, etc.) **except** as expressly permitted in Section 2A(a) (public API use, paid subscription, no separate license needed) and Section 2A(b-i) (closed-source self-hosting under a paid Commercial License) or Section 2A(b-ii) (full-OSS self-hosting)
* Integrating the Software into a paid product, platform, or commercial offering **except** as permitted in Sections 2A(a) and 2A(b)
* Using the Software for commercial consulting, client work, or agency deliverables
* Any activity that generates revenue, directly or indirectly, using the Software **except** as permitted in Sections 2A(a) and 2A(b)

