### 3. Commercial Use — What Requires Permission and What Does Not

* **No separate OCL Commercial License is required** to use Oxiverse's API or hosted services for **any** purpose, including commercial purposes (Section 2A(a)) — you simply pay the applicable subscription (a free tier is available for personal and research use). Your independent product is not a derivative work of the Software.
* **Self-hosted commercial deployment** is permitted under either: (i) a **paid Commercial License** that allows closed-source operation (Section 2A(b-i)); or (ii) the **free full-OSS path** where the entire stack is open-sourced under OCL with no open-washing (Section 2A(b-ii) & 3A). Self-hosting for Non-Commercial Purposes needs no license (Section 2).
* **Closed-source self-hosting requires a paid Commercial License.** A closed-source/proprietary self-hosting deployment is permitted **only** under a paid Commercial License obtained from Licensor (Section 2A(b-i), Section 2A(d)). The full-OSS self-hosting path (Section 2A(b-ii) & 3A) is the free alternative.
* Licensor **DOES** issue paid Commercial Licenses, including the **closed-source self-hosting license** (Section 2A(b-i)) and enhanced hosted-service licenses (white-label, redistribution of the hosted service, SLA, support, custom development) — these are available to any party on request (Section 2A(d)). The only self-hosting path that is free is the full-OSS one (Section 2A(b-ii) & 3A); a closed-source self-hosting license is a paid product, not a free grant.

To confirm compliance for an open-source project, contact: **[likhith@oxiverse.com](mailto:likhith@oxiverse.com)**.

