Any contribution submitted to Licensor for inclusion in the Software shall be under the terms and conditions of this License. Contributions become part of the Software licensed under OCL v1.x and may not be relicensed by any party outside the terms of this License. By submitting a contribution, you represent that:

* (a) You have the right to license it under OCL v1.x;
* (b) You grant Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive license to use, modify, and distribute your contribution under this License.

**Compensation:** Contributions are voluntary. Oxiverse does **not** pay contributors for code, documentation, or other submissions. By submitting a contribution you agree it is provided without expectation of payment.

**Contributor Monetization:** Contributors may monetize their own use of the Software exactly like any other party, via either path in Section 2A(b):
  * (i) **Buy a paid closed-source Commercial License** (Section 2A(b-i)) — contributors are eligible for an **extra contributor discount**; contact **[likhith@oxiverse.com](mailto:likhith@oxiverse.com)**; or
  * (ii) **Self-host commercially for FREE** by releasing the ENTIRE stack under OCL or an OSI-approved open source license with no open-washing (Section 2A(b-ii) & 3A).
Contributors are **not** granted a free closed-source self-hosting license; the discount applies only to the paid license.

**Oxiverse's use of contributions.** Oxiverse may use, modify, and distribute your contribution in its own offerings without additional compensation. Oxiverse does **not**, however, place externally-contributed code into any deployment that remains closed-source / proprietary. Accordingly, contributed code is included in Oxiverse's offerings only where the Oxiverse service incorporating it is released under OCL or an OSI-approved open source license (Section 2A(b-ii) & 3A). Oxiverse operates its proprietary hosted service/API and sells paid Commercial Licenses under its own rights as Licensor using Oxiverse-authored code; those offerings are outside the scope of this restriction (see Section 2A(a): the hosted service/API is a separate paid offering and is not licensed under OCL).

**Contributor Rights.** In addition to the rights above, every contributor receives the following benefits with respect to their own contribution:

* **(i) Royalty-free reuse of your own contribution.** You retain the right to use, modify, and redistribute your contributed code in any context (your own projects, other products, commercial or non-commercial) without royalty or further permission from Oxiverse. This right covers your contribution only and does not grant any right to the rest of the Oxiverse Software or to other contributors' work.
* **(ii) Credit in distributions.** Oxiverse will credit you in releases and public distributions that include your contribution, subject to a privacy opt-out (a contributor may request omission of their name by contacting **[likhith@oxiverse.com](mailto:likhith@oxiverse.com)**). Credit obligations apply only to distributions that contain the contribution.
* **(iii) Additional licensing of your contribution.** You may license your own contribution under other terms (including an OSI-approved open source license such as MIT, Apache 2.0, or GPL) separately and elsewhere. Any such separate licensing is additional only: your grant of OCL rights to Oxiverse in subsection (b) is perpetual and irrevocable and is not withdrawn by any other license you grant.
* **(iv) Royalty-free commercial reuse of your own contribution.** Contributors retain royalty-free rights to use their own contribution in their own separate commercial works without a paid Commercial License, provided the work does not incorporate other Oxiverse services beyond that contribution. For commercial self-hosting of the full Oxiverse stack (including other contributors' code) in closed-source form, contributors remain eligible for the paid closed-source Commercial License at the contributor discount in subsection (i) above — there is no free closed-source self-hosting grant.

All Oxiverse services and the core Oxiverse Software — including its cognitive architecture (RAVANA, RLMv2, ConceptGraph, and successor components) — remain under OCL v1.x and may not be relicensed, sublicensed, or closed-sourced by any party, including contributors. Only derivative works and original extensions created on top of the core may be commercialized under proprietary terms, subject to a valid paid Commercial License (Section 2A(b-i) & 2A(d)).

